WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.602
The Trump White House
is panicking

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.737
as the midterm election results
get worse

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.706
and the Russia
investigation looms.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:09.842
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:13.780
♪♪

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.448
It's not unusual to see turnover

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:18.418
in presidential administrations
after a midterm election,

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.486
but this White House
has already seen

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:22.855
an unprecedented level
of turnover

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.256
even before the elections,

00:00:24.256 --> 00:00:26.192
and apparently
there's a lot more coming.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.827
-President Trump
reportedly ready

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.930
to fire Homeland Security
Secretary Kirstjen Nielsen.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.366
-NBC News is learning
that White House Chief of Staff

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:36.602
John Kelly might be leaving
the West Wing soon.

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:38.838
-Sarah Sanders, for example,
has been someone

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.173
who has been there actually
for quite some time

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:42.875
and might be headed out.

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:44.277
-Others rumored to be leaving

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.445
include Commerce Secretary
Wilbur Ross

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:50.517
and Interior Secretary
Ryan Zinke.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.952
-Damn. Is there anyone left?

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.254
Trump is slowly turning
the White House

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:57.323
into the Overlook Hotel.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.891
Pretty soon it'll just be Trump

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:02.028
in a ratty bathrobe
writing all over the walls.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:04.864
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.167
[ Applause ]

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.302
You can tell -- You can tell the
midterm results were way worse

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.803
for Republicans
than they initially let on

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:12.238
from the way they're behaving.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.807
And the more results we get from
last week's midterm elections,

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:18.344
the clearer it is that this was
in fact a massive blue wave,

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.814
even though in the immediate
aftermath of the election,

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:22.448
Trump tried to make it sound

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:24.817
like all the candidates
he supported won.

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:27.987
-We saw the candidates
that I supported

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:31.457
achieve tremendous success
last night.

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:34.794
-Last night was not
an absolute victory for you.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.463
-I'll be honest.
I thought it was a --

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:41.166
I thought it was a very close
to complete victory.

00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:42.535
I think it was a great victory.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.704
I'll be honest.
I think it was a great victory.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:48.508
-I love that thing Trump does
where he, in real time,

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.743
talks himself into
bragging about something

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.246
he knows is a failure.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.081
It's like
he's psyching himself up

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.949
to ask a girl to a school dance.

00:01:56.949 --> 00:02:00.586
"I'm an okay-looking guy.
I mean, honestly, I'm handsome.

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.855
If I'm being honest,
I'm the most handsome man
who ever lived.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:05.491
Okay, I'm ready.
Hello, cheerleader!"

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:07.560
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.228
In reality, Trump intervened

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.397
in a series of races
where his candidates lost.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.332
He campaigned repeatedly
in Montana

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:16.068
against Democratic Senator
Jon Tester, who won re-election,

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:17.670
and he flew to Nevada

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.473
to campaign for defeated
Senator Dean Heller,

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.074
where his main contribution

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:23.810
was coming up
with a super-dumb nickname

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.545
for Jacky Rosen,
Heller's Democratic opponent.

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:30.583
-I have to tell you. His
opponent wants to raise taxes.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.351
[ Crowd boos ]

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:34.720
-And take our guns!
-She wants to raise taxes.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.691
Think of it.
I mean, it's ridiculous.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:41.193
Should I mention her name
or should I not?

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:42.361
Huh?

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:44.531
[ Crowd shouting and jeering ]

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:47.400
I have a great nickname for her,
actually, but I'm not gonna...

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.769
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.272
[ Crowd shouting and jeering ]

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.745
No. We shouldn't do it.

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:01.747
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:06.252
All right. I won't do it.
Wacky Jacky.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:09.188
-Ugh!

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:14.126
What a long wait
for a huge disappointment.

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:18.164
That's like waiting
for a kid to show you a dive.

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:21.733
"Okay.

00:03:21.733 --> 00:03:25.537
Okay. We're all watching.

00:03:25.537 --> 00:03:29.809
Yep! Yeah. We can see you, bud.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:36.082
All right, bud, let's see it.

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:39.185
Any second, bud. Come on, now.

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:42.221
Oh, all right. Yeah.

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:44.857
Great dive, bud."

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.159
Although I do think if she
really wanted to troll Trump,

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:49.362
she should totally use that
as her official title.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:52.432
That would make calling her
Senate office a lot more fun.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:56.335
-Hello. You have reached the
office of Senator Wacky Jacky.

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:59.037
For constituent services,
press 1.

00:03:59.037 --> 00:04:01.507
For legislation, press 2.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:06.278
For wacky behavior including
goofs, gags, spoofs, pranks,

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:09.848
whimsy, wise cracks,
japes, jests,

00:04:09.848 --> 00:04:12.818
horseplay,
and general tomfoolery,

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:14.053
press 3.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:17.256
And to hear the sound of a fart,
press 4.

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:18.724
[ Beep ]

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:20.626
[ Flatulence ]

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:25.464
-And then, of course, Trump
also intervened in Arizona,

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:28.134
where he antagonized
Republican Senator Jeff Flake

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:29.902
and tried to force him
out of the race

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.571
by encouraging
a primary challenger.

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:33.072
In fact, Trump even bragged

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:35.741
that he was the reason
Flake chose to retire.

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:39.779
-We also had a staggering number
of House retirements.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.047
So it's a little tough.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.982
-You said that many of the
retirements that happened

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.450
in the House
made it very difficult --

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.918
-Many retirements, yeah.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:48.621
-That made it very difficult
for you in this election cycle,

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:49.889
and that it was because

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.091
they were chairmanships
that were vacated,

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:54.627
but Jeff Flake wasn't
a chairman of a committee,

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.628
and Paul Ryan
also retired this cycle.

00:04:56.628 --> 00:04:59.365
So, why do you think that is?
Whose fault is it that --

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.767
-In Jeff Flake's case,
it's me, pure and simple.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.769
I retired him.
-Oh, my God.

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:06.038
He sounds like he's auditioning

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:09.942
for the role of a two-bit thug
on "Ray Donovan."

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:12.178
"What happened to Three Thumbs
Joey? Did he pay up?"

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:16.782
"Let's just say he didn't have
the cash, so I retired him."

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:18.584
But, hey, say what you will
about Trump.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.953
When he intervenes in a race,
he gets the results he wants.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.322
So, who's the new
Trump-friendly Republican

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:24.857
who replaced Flake
in the Senate?

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:26.826
-An historic victory
out of Arizona.

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:28.294
Democrat Kyrsten Sinema

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:30.896
prevailed over Republican
Martha McSally,

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:34.567
making her the first Democratic
senator elected by the state

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.068
in three decades.

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:38.637
-So Trump bragged about
getting a Republican to retire,

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:41.140
and then that Republican
was replaced by a Democrat

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:44.843
who is also the first
openly bisexual senator.

00:05:44.843 --> 00:05:48.247
This is a case
where Trump's like a guy

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:50.016
who doesn't get along
with his buddy's girlfriend,

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:51.517
so he convinces him to dump her.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:54.186
And then his buddy brings his
new girlfriend over for dinner,

00:05:54.186 --> 00:05:57.756
and when Trump opens the door,
it's Hillary Clinton.

00:05:57.756 --> 00:06:00.192
"Ha ha! Hello, Donald!

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:03.128
It's me, Hillary, and I'm
dating your new best friend!

00:06:03.128 --> 00:06:05.564
Ha ha ha!"

00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:07.867
So as the results get worse
for Republicans,

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:09.869
they're getting more desperate,
and they seem to be focusing

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:11.270
their desperation on Florida,

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.005
where governor and Senate
candidate Rick Scott

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:15.374
has been spreading
baseless conspiracy theories

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:17.343
about voter fraud
amid a recount there

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:18.911
in an incredibly tight race.

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:20.947
And now he and his lawyers
won't even say

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:23.516
that they'll accept the results
as legitimate if he loses.

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:26.419
-Every Floridian
should be concerned

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:29.088
there may be rampant fraud
happening

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:30.890
in Palm Beach
and Broward Counties.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:34.627
Senator Nelson is clearly
trying to commit fraud

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.161
to try to win this election.

00:06:36.161 --> 00:06:37.329
That's all this is.

00:06:37.329 --> 00:06:40.566
-If, after the recount,
somehow --

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:41.968
and I know it's unlikely --

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:44.770
but somehow Bill Nelson
were to prevail,

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:47.339
would Rick Scott,
who is the governor right now,

00:06:47.339 --> 00:06:48.540
certify that election?

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.042
And he wouldn't say yes.

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.477
So, you've had a night
to think about it.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:52.878
So is the answer
this morning yes?

00:06:52.878 --> 00:06:54.580
-Well, I'm also not going to
answer whether Rick Scott's

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.782
gonna win the Heisman Trophy,
because he's not.

00:06:56.782 --> 00:06:59.284
-"And I'm also not going to
answer whether Rick Scott

00:06:59.284 --> 00:07:01.888
escaped from the Bodies exhibit,
'cause he didn't."

00:07:01.888 --> 00:07:04.290
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.659
[ Applause ]

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:10.195
So, Republicans
have been spreading lies

00:07:10.195 --> 00:07:12.465
about nonexistent voter fraud
without any evidence,

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:14.567
and you'll never guess
who they're blaming

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.835
for that nonexistent
voter fraud.

00:07:16.835 --> 00:07:19.538
-Rudy Giuliani is pointing
the blame at Hillary Clinton,

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:22.608
writing Hillary's lawyers trying
to steal Florida election.

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:24.677
They are still counting
or creating ballots

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:26.846
just in Democratic
Broward and Palm Beach.

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:30.516
-People should be suspicious
when Hillary Clinton's lawyer,

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:33.119
who paid for
Russian information,

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:36.088
is involved
in any election recount.

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:37.890
-And now they are finding votes.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.925
And you have this guy Elias,

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:44.764
who represented Hillary Clinton
in a lot of very shady things.

00:07:44.764 --> 00:07:46.765
-Here's really
something frightening.

00:07:46.765 --> 00:07:49.135
The lawyer who's representing
Senator Nelson,

00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:51.470
the Democrat incumbent,
his name is Marc Elias.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:52.871
Does that sound familiar?

00:07:52.871 --> 00:07:54.707
That's the same lawyer
Hillary Clinton hired

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:58.077
to get that Russian dossier
created two years ago.

00:07:58.077 --> 00:08:00.045
-Oh, my God.
They talk about Hillary Clinton

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:03.715
like the Crypt Keeper teeing up
the next horror movie.

00:08:03.715 --> 00:08:05.584
"Hello, boils and ghouls!

00:08:05.584 --> 00:08:07.086
Here's a terrifying tale

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:10.222
that will send a shiver
down your spine!

00:08:10.222 --> 00:08:14.060
The lawyer representing
Democrats in the Florida recount

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:18.030
worked for a firm that was
previously hired by...

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.832
Hillary Clinton!"

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:21.300
♪♪

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.202
[ Evil laughter ]

00:08:23.202 --> 00:08:27.340
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:29.841 --> 00:08:31.977
Why? Why is Trump freaking out?

00:08:31.977 --> 00:08:33.713
Well, he's reportedly
getting nervous

00:08:33.713 --> 00:08:35.581
because now that the elections
are over,

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:37.750
the special counsel
in the Russia investigation,

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.885
Robert Mueller,
can go back to indicting people

00:08:39.885 --> 00:08:41.153
and writing his final report.

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:42.821
We've heard very little
from Mueller

00:08:42.821 --> 00:08:45.257
over the past few months,
leading to speculation

00:08:45.257 --> 00:08:47.192
over what his next move
might be.

00:08:47.192 --> 00:08:49.027
-He knows that the midterm
elections are over,

00:08:49.027 --> 00:08:52.297
and he knows the quiet time
that Mueller gave him

00:08:52.297 --> 00:08:53.699
is now going to get loud.

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:56.401
-A lot of speculation
on Robert Mueller,

00:08:56.401 --> 00:08:57.936
who has been quiet lately.

00:08:57.936 --> 00:08:59.472
-Mueller has been very quiet.

00:08:59.472 --> 00:09:03.041
-This has been a quiet time
for Robert Mueller.

00:09:03.041 --> 00:09:05.076
-Because Robert Mueller
has been quiet,

00:09:05.076 --> 00:09:08.747
we should assume that
he's been more busy than ever.

00:09:08.747 --> 00:09:10.149
-If you're Donald Trump,

00:09:10.149 --> 00:09:12.584
there's got to be
nothing more terrifying

00:09:12.584 --> 00:09:14.920
than hearing that Robert Mueller
has been quiet.

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.855
This guy is a Marine.

00:09:16.855 --> 00:09:18.491
He's probably spent
the last six months

00:09:18.491 --> 00:09:20.159
sneaking closer and closer.

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:22.295
At this point,
he's probably in camouflage

00:09:22.295 --> 00:09:25.064
that matches
the Oval Office drapes.

00:09:25.064 --> 00:09:26.698
[ Laughter ]

00:09:26.698 --> 00:09:28.567
For two years,
Trump has acted like a guy

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:30.436
who's afraid the walls
are closing in,

00:09:30.436 --> 00:09:32.504
and that was when Republicans
were in charge of everything.

00:09:32.504 --> 00:09:35.374
Now Democrats control the House,
and Mueller can make news again.

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:38.177
Although if Mueller ever issues
a public statement about Trump,

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:40.812
he'll probably just say...
-I retired him.

00:09:40.812 --> 00:09:43.215
-This has been "A Closer Look."

